---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { services } from '../lib/repo';
import { site } from '../config';

const unverified = services().filter((s) => s.tested !== 'verified');
---
<Guide
  page="contribute"
  lede="Cupola is open source under the Apache License 2.0. The most useful thing you can send us is a report from a service you run, whether it worked or not."
  related={['services', 'press', 'install']}
  get={false}
>
  <h2>Report from your own stack</h2>
  <p>Every integration follows the service's official API and has tests. Only a real server shows whether it works with your setup. These are not fully verified yet:</p>
  <ul>
    {unverified.map((s) => (
      <li><a href={`/services/${s.id}/`}>{s.name}</a>: {s.tested === 'partial' ? 'partly verified' : 'recorded answers only'}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p><a href={`${site.issues}/new`} rel="noopener">Open an issue</a> with the service, its version, how you reach it, and what you saw. “It works” is as useful to us as “it does not”.</p>

  <h2>Accessibility</h2>
  <p>Large text, contrast, touch targets and screen readers are covered by tests. Something that reads badly with VoiceOver or TalkBack is a bug: please report it.</p>

  <h2>Code and integrations</h2>
  <p>Open an issue first, so we agree on the plan before you write code. Setup and conventions are in <a href={site.contributing} rel="noopener">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>, and the design system is in <code>design/</code>.</p>

  <h2>Help other people find it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={site.repo} rel="noopener">Star the repository</a>, so people on GitHub can find it.</li>
    <li>Tell people who run the same stack: your Discord, your forum, the thread asking for a Sonarr app.</li>
    <li>Writing about it? The <a href="/press/">press kit</a> has descriptions, the mark and the facts.</li>
    <li>If it helps you, a donation on <a href={site.kofi} rel="noopener">Ko-fi</a> keeps it moving.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>
